/-!
# Regularity and derivations

Stacks Project, Chapter 15 "More on Algebra". The tags treated here are

07PF, 0GEE, 07PG, 07PH, 07PI, 07PJ.

## Tag 07PF — Regular hypersurface quotients detected by a derivation

Let `R` be a regular ring and `f : R`. If a derivation of `R` sends `f` to a unit
modulo the principal ideal generated by `f`, then the hypersurface ring `R/(f)` is
regular.

### Main definitions

There are no new definitions.

### Main results

* `isRegularRing_quotient_span_singleton_of_isUnit_derivation`: the
  Jacobian criterion for a hypersurface quotient expressed using a derivation.

### Implementation notes

An ordinary derivation of a commutative ring is represented as a derivation over
`ℤ`. The quotient `R/(f)` is represented by `R ⧸ Ideal.span {f}`. The derivation
witness is an explicit argument, the curried form of the existential hypothesis in
the source.

### References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 07PF](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/07PF)

## Tag 0GEE — Regular quotients detected by a matrix of derivations

Let `R` be a regular local ring and let `f` be a finite family in its maximal ideal. If there is
a family of derivations of `R` for which the matrix of values on `f` has unit determinant, then
the quotient by `f` is regular local and `f` is a regular sequence.

### Main definitions

There are no new definitions.

### Main results

* `isRegularLocalRing_quotient_span_range_and_isRegular_of_isUnit_det_derivation`:
  the derivation criterion for a finite family in a regular local ring.

### Implementation notes

An ordinary derivation of a commutative ring is represented as a derivation over `ℤ`. The finite
family is indexed by `Fin m`, its generated ideal is `Ideal.span (Set.range f)`, and its ordered
regular-sequence assertion uses `List.ofFn f`. The statement also includes the empty family,
where the determinant and both conclusions hold canonically.

### References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 0GEE](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0GEE)

## Tag 07PG — Regularity of polynomial hypersurfaces detected by a derivation

Let `R` be a regular ring and let `f : R`. If a derivation of `R` sends `f` to a
unit, then adjoining a root of `p - f` gives a regular ring for every polynomial
`p` with integer coefficients.

### Main definitions

There are no new definitions.

### Main results

* `isRegularRing_quotient_polynomial_sub_C_of_isUnit_derivation`: the
  quotient of `R[X]` by `p(X) - f` is regular when a derivation sends `f` to a unit.

### Implementation notes

An ordinary derivation is represented as a derivation over `ℤ`, and an integer
polynomial is transported to `R[X]` along `algebraMap ℤ R`. The general statement
includes the source's assertion about `X ^ n - C f` for positive `n`.

### References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 07PG](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/07PG)

## Tag 07PH — Derivations detecting non-p-th-powers

Let `B` be a domain of prime characteristic that is of finite type over a Noetherian complete
local ring. Every element of `B` that is not a p-th power in its fraction field is detected by
an ordinary derivation of `B`.

### Main definitions

There are no new definitions.

### Main results

* `exists_derivation_apply_ne_zero_of_not_pow_fractionRing`: an element that is not a
  p-th power in the fraction field has nonzero image under some derivation of `B`.

### Implementation notes

The fraction field is represented abstractly by `IsFractionRing`, completeness means adic
completeness for the maximal ideal, and an ordinary derivation is represented as a derivation
over `ℤ`.

### References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 07PH](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/07PH)

## Tag 07PI — Complete local domains are J-0

A Noetherian local domain that is complete for its maximal-ideal-adic topology has a nonempty
open subset of its spectrum on which all local rings are regular.

### Main definitions

There are no new definitions.

### Main results

* `isJ0_of_isPrecomplete_maximalIdeal`: a Noetherian complete local domain is J-0.

### Implementation notes

Completeness is stated as precompleteness for the maximal ideal. For a Noetherian local ring,
separatedness is automatic, so this is equivalent to the source's adic completeness hypothesis.

### References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 07PI](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/07PI)

## Tag 07PJ — Standard classes of J-2 rings

Fields, Noetherian complete local rings, the integers, one-dimensional Noetherian local rings,
one-dimensional Nagata rings, and Dedekind domains of characteristic zero are J-2. The J-2
property is also preserved by finite type ring extensions.

### Main definitions

There are no new definitions.

### Main results

* `isJ2_of_standard_classes_and_finiteType` gives the standard classes of J-2 rings
  and stability under finite type extensions.

### Implementation notes

Completeness of a Noetherian local ring is expressed by precompleteness for its maximal ideal;
separatedness is automatic in this setting. For a domain, characteristic zero is equivalent to
characteristic zero of its fraction field. The seven assertions in the source are packaged as a
single conjunction.

### References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 07PJ](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/07PJ)

-/

